# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .gitignore — copied here at scaffold from the Brain's
# Projects/(PROJECT TEMPLATE)/_gitignore-template
#
# POLICY (decided 2026-08-18): the remote carries the app and the design docs a
# technical reader would want. It does NOT carry solo-work internals — the running
# project log, internal planning docs, agent/skill tooling, or the project's
# CLAUDE.md. Those stay local, in the Obsidian vault where the rest of the system
# can see them.
#
# Decide this at commit 1. Adding a path here later does nothing to files git is
# already tracking (that needs `git rm -r --cached`), and even then every old
# version stays in history forever unless you rewrite it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Solo-work internals — local only ────────────────────────────────────────
# The append-only master log + raw run dumps. Internal narrative, disposable test
# accounts, no external value.
# ⚠ This is the file that carries project history across sessions. Ignoring it
#   means git is no longer its backup — make sure the vault itself is backed up.
notes-logs/

# Internal planning docs: ROADMAP, IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN_<phase>, cost diagnoses.
# The public design docs (ARCHITECTURE, TECH_STACK, DATABASE_SCHEMA, GLOSSARY,
# DATA_HANDLING, UI_DESIGN, UI_WORKFLOW) stay in docs/ and stay tracked.
docs/internal/

# Project-scoped Claude instructions. Documents personal working style and process
# history, not the codebase. AGENTS.md (if the stack generates one) stays tracked.
CLAUDE.md

# Agent/skill tooling. Mostly vendored third-party skill content — not ours to
# redistribute, and irrelevant to anyone reading the code.
# NOTE: .claude/skills/ contains symlinks INTO .agents/skills/. Ignore both or
#       neither — ignoring one leaves dangling symlinks in a fresh clone.
# NOTE: skills-lock.json (repo root) is NOT ignored — it's the reinstall manifest.
.claude/
.agents/

# If this ever stops being solo work, un-ignoring shared project settings is a
# one-line change:
# !.claude/settings.json

# ── Explicitly TRACKED (listed here so nobody "tidies" them away) ───────────
# design-system/    ← the token spec globals.css implements; the *why* behind
#                     every color and font, with provenance + contrast reasoning
# docs/             ← public design docs (see docs/internal/ above for the split)
# skills-lock.json  ← manifest for reinstalling the .agents/ skills
# README.md         ← the repo's public face

# ── Editor / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Obsidian session state. Shared config is not worth the churn in a code repo.
.obsidian
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem

# MCP server config. Holds the 21st.dev API key in plaintext.
# This repo is the source of a PUBLIC website — a leaked key here is a leaked key
# forever, since old versions stay in history. Added 2026-08-27, BEFORE connecting
# 21st.dev, per the roadmap's Phase 1 ordering.
# Verify with:  git grep 21st_sk_ -- ':!.gitignore'   (must return nothing)
# The pathspec excludes this file — without it the check matches its own
# documentation and always "fails", which trains you to ignore it.
.mcp.json

# ── Node / Next.js ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/node_modules
/.next/
/out/
/build
/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.vercel
